# Changelog

All notable changes to the **Z2Z (Zimbra2Zimbra Migration Tool)** project are documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

---

## [1.0.3] - 2026-08-27

### 🚀 Highlights

- **Complete English Localization**: Fully translated all shell scripts, console feedback, interactive prompts, and documentation from Portuguese to standard English.
- **Modern ASCII Banner & Identity**: Refreshed ASCII terminal branding with **alsyundawy** art and standardized version metadata.
- **Code Hardening & ShellCheck Compliance**: Refactored helper routines, variable expansions, and sourcing patterns to achieve 100% linter and static analysis compliance.
- **Documentation Architecture**: Rebuilt documentation with standardized headings, quickstart guides, compatibility specifications, and clean markdown structures.

### 🌐 Localization & User Experience

- Standardized all user-facing prompts (`Continue (yes/no)?`, `Replace hostname?`, `Export mailboxes?`) with consistent confirmation handling.
- Enhanced terminal output styling with structured color palettes for errors, warnings, successes, and status markers.
- Added comprehensive English descriptions for Class of Service (COS), account filters, alias maps, and distribution list export routines.

### 🛠️ Code Quality & Reliability

- Added `# shellcheck` annotations and safe variable expansion (`${zimbra_server_hostname:-}`) for dynamic runtime variables sourced via `zmsetvars`.
- Standardized file descriptor redirection using `: > "${file}"` syntax to avoid ShellCheck SC2188 warnings.
- Isolated command executions in subshells and variable captures to avoid masking return codes.
- Verified zero errors across 6 integrated linters (`git-diff-check`, `markdownlint`, `prettier`, `shellcheck`, `shfmt`, `trufflehog`).

### 📚 Documentation

- Overhauled [README.md](README.md) with dedicated sections: Overview, Quickstart, Dependencies, Configuration, Running Tests, What Will Be Migrated, User Feedback, Roadmap, Contributing, and License.
- Revamped [INSTALL](INSTALL) with step-by-step guides for single-server and multi-server environments.
- Enriched subdirectory guides in [export/README.md](export/README.md), [skell/README.md](skell/README.md), and [util/README.md](util/README.md).

---

## [1.0.2] - 2024-03-15

### ⚠️ Improvements

- Added administrative pre-flight warnings for multi-server environments containing more than one active Mailbox server.

---

## [1.0.1] - 2023-11-20

### 🔄 Changes

- Expanded distribution list LDAP export query to include `zimbraGroup` object class entries in addition to standard distribution lists.

---

## [1.0.0c] - 2022-08-10

### 🧪 Compatibility

- Validated support for multi-server environments that do not require mailbox hostname replacement.

---

## [1.0.0b] - 2021-04-05

### ⚡ Performance & Data Integrity

- Added `-t 0` parameter to `zmmailbox` commands to eliminate timeout limits when archiving large mailboxes (>2GB).
- Switched default mailbox import strategy from `reset` (destructive overwrite) to `skip` (safe non-destructive merge).

---

## [1.0.0a] - 2020-09-18

### 🐛 Bug Fixes

- Fixed LDIF hostname comparison logic during pre-flight import checks.
- Introduced automated session logging (`session-<timestamp>.log`) to trace import operations.

---

## [0.9.9f] - 2019-12-14

### 🔒 Validation

- Added strict FQDN syntax validation when interactively entering replacement hostnames.
- Enforced hostname parity validation between local Zimbra server and imported LDIF records.
- Standardized environment discovery through native Zimbra environment variables.

---

## [0.9.9c] - 2018-06-22

### ✨ Features

- Added interactive toggle allowing administrators to choose whether to export/import the `admin` user account.
- Added default alias exclusions to preserve native `root` and `postmaster` system aliases.

---

## [0.9.9] - 2017-02-10

### 🚀 Initial Release

- Core export/import pipeline for Class of Service (Default & DefaultExternal), user accounts, aliases, and distribution lists.
- Built-in exclusion filters for internal Zimbra system accounts (spam, ham, virus quarantine, galsync).
- Batch script generation for full mailbox archive exports via `zmmailbox`.
